  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Evening Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    31 July 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good evening Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,218.38/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,216.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SIGMUND</td>\n                <td>₦1,222.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SHEMA</td>\n                <td>₦1,216.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,216.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ARDOVA</td>\n                <td>₦1,217.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SOROMAN</td>\n                <td>₦1,220.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SOBAZ</td>\n                <td>₦1,220.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MAINLAND</td>\n                <td>₦1,220.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,633.75/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AITEO</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Nigeria Removes Import Duty, VAT on Fully Gas-Powered, Electric Vehicles\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Vehicles running on compressed natural gas, liquefied petroleum gas or electric power will now enter Nigeria free of import duty and Value Added Tax. The exemption covers vehicles running entirely on CNG or LPG, battery electric vehicles, and Extended Range Electric Vehicles able to travel at least 200 kilometres on battery power alone. Hybrids remain excluded, along with dual fuel vehicles still running partly on petrol or diesel.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nigeria-removes-import-duty-vat-on-fully-gas-powered-electric-vehicles\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NNPCL Confirms Deployment of Over 1,000 Graduate Trainees After One-Year Programme\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Nigerian National Petroleum Company Limited (NNPCL) has confirmed the deployment of more than 1,000 young professionals into its workforce. The milestone was announced by the Group Chief Executive Officer of NNPCL, Bayo Ojulari. He described the exercise as part of the company's ongoing efforts to build a skilled and performance-driven workforce.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nnpcl-confirms-deployment-of-over-1000-graduate-trainees-after-one-year-programme\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Seplat to Sell 10% JV Stake to NNPC in $281.6m Deal, Retains Operatorship\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Seplat Energy Plc has entered into a binding agreement to divest a 10 percent working interest in its joint venture assets to the Nigerian National Petroleum Company Limited. The agreement takes effect from April 1, 2026. Seplat said proceeds from the transaction will strengthen its financial position, with about half earmarked for debt reduction.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/seplat-to-sell-10-jv-stake-to-nnpc-in-2816m-deal-retains-operatorship\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Why OTL Africa 2026 Is A Must-Attend Event for Energy Industry Professionals\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The 20th OTL Africa Downstream Energy Week is scheduled for October 25–30, 2026 in Lagos. The event will feature a conference and international exhibition from October 26 to 29, attracting regulators, government officials, investors, energy companies, technology providers and service firms.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/why-otl-africa-2026-is-a-must-attend-event-for-energy-industry-professionals\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Nigeria's Refining Capacity Could Hit 2.6m bpd by 2030\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria's domestic refining capacity could rise to 2.64 million barrels per day by the end of 2030. 24 new refinery projects progress through various stages of development. $10.74 billion worth of investments in modular refinery projects are expected to be completed between 2026 and 2030.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nigerias-refining-capacity-could-hit-26m-bpd-by-2030\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
